17592186045417] [17592186050293 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050293 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050293 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050293 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050293 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050293 #edb/ref 1031 "Tangent Planes to Surfaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050293 #edb/ref 1033 1980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050293 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "3d717848-5743-5882-aa66-adea2ee38d55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1031 "The Cartesian Equation of a Plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1033 1807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050830 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6a093d52-40f2-54b8-8982-db428e58bab5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050991 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050991 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050991 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186147425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050991 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186147426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050991 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186147427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050991 #edb/ref 1031 "The Intersection of Two Planes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050991 #edb/ref 1033 2539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050991 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051046 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051046 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051046 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051046 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051046 #edb/ref 1031 "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051046 #edb/ref 1033 1853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051046 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7cf616eb-2b54-52d2-8407-1b2fc912b2d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119643 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4936" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119643 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(9,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}=3\\mathbf{i}-4\\mathbf{j}+7\\mathbf{k}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119643 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "01f32313-178c-5626-91af-110907202416" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119643 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle 9,-2,3 \\rangle$ and the normal vector of the plane is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 3,-4,7 \\rangle.$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,7⟩ & =⟨9,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,7⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,7⟩ & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $\\mathbf{r}=\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,7⟩ & =56 \\\\ 3x-4y+7z & =56 \\\\ 3x-4y+7z-56 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119644 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4937" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119644 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-1,4,8)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\dfrac{x+3}{-5}=\\dfrac{y-1}{3}=\\dfrac{z+2}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119644 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d92eb242-104f-55cd-82dc-7620e2f4e636" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119644 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -1,4,8 \\rangle.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $\\langle -5,3,2 \\rangle.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\langle -5,3,2 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,3,2⟩ & =⟨-1,4,8⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,3,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,3,2⟩ & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $\\mathbf{r}=\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,3,2⟩ & =33 \\\\ -5x+3y+2z & =33 \\\\ -5x+3y+2z-33 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119645 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4938" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119645 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the Cartesian equation $2x-y+z+13=0$ of the plane $\\Pi,$ find an equation of $\\Pi$ in the form $(\\mathbf{r}-\\mathbf{p})\\cdot\\mathbf{n}=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119645 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa7c3400-9bc0-5f3a-84e5-f3cc2bb87f5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119645 #edb/ref 1074 "First, from the coefficients in equation of the plane, we get that the normal vector of $\\Pi$ is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 2,-1,1 \\rangle.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $\\Pi$ for $z\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z+13 & =0 \\\\ z & =-2x+y-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0,$ we get $z=-13.$ So, the point $P(0,0,-13)$ lies on $\\Pi.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle 0,0,-13 \\rangle.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,-1,1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119646 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4939" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119646 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,2,-6)$ and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{v_1}=\\langle -3, 5, 2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}=\\langle 1, 3, -2 \\rangle.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119646 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a9e1070-0ca0-5f24-ac89-999c9271a91b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119646 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,-6 \\rangle.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $\\mathbf{v_1}$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-16i-4j-14k \\\\  & =⟨-16,-4,-14⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-16,-4,-14⟩ & =⟨-3,2,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨-16,-4,-14⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-16,-4,-14⟩ & =124\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $\\mathbf{r}=\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-16,-4,-14⟩ & =124 \\\\ -16x-4y-14z & =124 \\\\ -16x-4y-14z-124 & =0 \\\\ 8x+2y+7z+62 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186314765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Cartesian Equation of the Plane Perpendicular To a Given Vector" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119832 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b34272b7-a7ad-5a58-974e-54cca957d06e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119833 #edb/re